{#
	 ============================================================
		FLAT TOGGLE (OFFCANVAS)  —  src/_includes/flat-toggle-offcanvas.njk
	 ============================================================

	 Single-button binary toggle for the .flat utility.
	 Composes with any theme — you can use Flat together with
	 Light, Dark, or any of the High Contrast modes.

	 Wired up by flat-toggle.js, which:
	   - listens on [data-flat-toggle]
	   - flips aria-pressed (+ .active)
	   - swaps the icon (bi-square ⇄ bi-square-fill)

	 The label stays "Flat mode" in both states. A toggle button
	 says its state through aria-pressed ("Flat mode, toggle button,
	 pressed"); the old label that changed to "Flat: On" / "Flat: Off"
	 announced the state twice (WAI-ARIA APG button pattern).

	 ON/OFF SWITCH: site.json → flatToggle: false hides this button,
	 drops flat-toggle.js from the bundle and makes theme-init.njk
	 stop applying a saved "flat", so nobody is stuck in flat mode.
	 The check sits here (not around the include in
	 offcanvas-menu.njk) so the partial switches itself off.
	 `!== false` = on unless explicitly turned off, so a site.json
	 without the key keeps the toggle.

	 Included by offcanvas-menu.njk, between the theme toggle
	 and the Bootswatch switcher.
	 ============================================================
#}

{% if site.flatToggle !== false %}
<div class="dd-offcanvas-divider"></div>
<div class="dd-offcanvas-section">
	<i class="bi bi-bounding-box me-1" aria-hidden="true"></i> Flat Mode
</div>
<div class="px-3 pb-3">
	<button type="button"
			class="btn btn-sm dd-btn-ghost w-100"
			data-flat-toggle
			aria-pressed="false">
		<i class="bi bi-square me-1" aria-hidden="true"></i> Flat mode
	</button>
</div>
{% endif %}
